From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 03 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: report Valgrind log on any failure

License: GPL-3.0-or-later
Upstream-Status: not-submitted
Origin: openEuler RISC-V packaging

Valgrind writes its diagnostics to a temporary work file which test-env.sh
deletes when each test exits.  The existing helper copies that file only for
the configured memory-error exit status 125.  If Valgrind itself cannot start,
or if the wrapped program returns another nonzero status, the actionable text
is therefore lost.

Print at most 2,000 lines of the temporary log to the per-test output for every
nonzero status before cleanup.  Preserve the existing memory-error handling
and return status, so this change neither skips nor converts a failing test.

This diagnostic gap was observed in exact-head openEuler RISC-V Package CI run
33707672244 for commit cbaff73805392e1fdc0e5d17e82c99db297bd30c.

---
 tests/run-valgrind.sh | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/run-valgrind.sh b/tests/run-valgrind.sh
--- a/tests/run-valgrind.sh
+++ b/tests/run-valgrind.sh
@@ -74,3 +74,14 @@ runWithValgrind () {
-	returnValue=$?
-
-	if test "${returnValue}" -eq 125; then
+	returnValue=$?
+
+	if test "${returnValue}" -ne 0; then
+		{
+		echo "================================================"
+		echo "Valgrind command failed with status ${returnValue}:"
+		echo "${testSubject} $*"
+		echo
+		sed -n '1,2000p' "${workFile4}"
+		echo "================================================"
+		} 1>&4
+	fi
+
+	if test "${returnValue}" -eq 125; then
